    Software with a paid offering to charge indirectly for the Software.

(b) Use, incorporate, modify, or distribute the Software to provide to
    third parties a product or service that competes with Workbench. A
    competing offering is one that provides Workbench's visual source-code
    authoring or editing functionality as a substitute for Workbench.
    This restriction applies to paid and free offerings, including hosted
    services, rebranded versions, plugins, and products based on modified
    or ported versions of the Software.

Internal use under section 2 is not, by itself, providing a competing
offering to third parties. Charging for work performed using the Software
or for outputs permitted under section 4 is not charging for the Software.
Merely using similar ideas in independently developed software that does
not use protected material from the Software is not restricted by this
